          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"flaubert-madame-bovary-5396f984c871\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.9,\"analysis\":\"The direct declaration “je vous aime” primarily avows a loving emotional state. Its placement after a plea to remain gives it a weak relational or commitment-invoking force, but it does not itself clearly undertake an obligation. The exclamation and urgency indicate intensity, not independently expressive/reflexive core force.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The narrow excerpt does not establish whether the avowal is sincere or strategically intended to prevent departure, but either reading remains principally truth-conditional in mode.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A character directly addresses another in represented dialogue: “De grâce, restez! je vous aime!”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The love avowal follows and reinforces an urgent request that the addressee stay. It may therefore function persuasively or as reassurance, but the local text does not show a distinct promise, relational undertaking, or reflex-like loss of verbal control. Sincerity and broader motives remain unresolved by the supplied excerpt.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"local-1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“je vous aime!”\",\"supports\":\"The conventional first-person declaration directly presents the speaker's love as true, strongly supporting T.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“De grâce, restez!” immediately precedes the declaration.\",\"supports\":\"The avowal is used to support an urgent plea that the addressee remain, giving limited support to relational invocation but not a clear undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"local-3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The utterance is exclamatory and occurs in an urgent appeal.\",\"supports\":\"This establishes emotional intensity and emphatic delivery, but supplies no independent evidence that the words are a reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.92}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T captures the avowal, while a small P score captures its limited use in pressing a relational appeal. Delivery and urgency can be handled contextually without E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":\"Classification is intentionally based only on the short supplied passage and metadata, without identifying the speaker or importing wider plot context.\"}"
